From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:48:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/44] qwen27: dump the vision tower's merged rows for a
 parity check

A vision port needs the tower's own output, not just the tokens it produces.
TF_QWEN_VISION_DUMP writes each image's merged rows beside the server, which is
what the reference harness captures from the merger.

Measured against transformers on this checkpoint, chart at 16x36 patches:
engine 144 rows x 4096, max 3.63, mean 3.9e-03, cos 0.99869, rms 0.2300 against
0.2299. So the tower's structure and scale are right and the per-row agreement is
high, but it is not bit-exact and the worst row differs by 3.6.

Served end to end on the same image: 164 prompt tokens, prefill 1397-1519 tok/s,
decode 30.7 tok/s, and answers that describe the chart and the photo.
